Our existing website for our home building business was recently ported to a WordPress installation -- where all of our content, photos and systems were transferred.

Now, with the new design in place -- we want an outside set of eyes to review the website and look for subtle/large changes that can help improve the usefulness of the website.

We do not want a full re-work. We want you to envision the current lay of the land... lay of the content... and visualize changes or additions to what is already there to make it better than it is. 

UX/UI is mainly what I'm after here. We want the ideas for improvement, not the actual improvements. We are ready to implement the changes, but we need your artistic direction from the outcome of this website review.

Direct scope of project: 

-- review all pages of website; 
-- determine areas that need improvement; 
-- create comments and specific instructions/text that accurately reflects the changes you see as better than what exists;
-- develop screen captures where those comments for improvement may be more directly tied to the existing website content;

*review of the website should be done on full desktop view and on mobile device resolutions;

*for general purpose of the website: we want to demo our homes, skills, and professionalism, and offer a convenient way for people to contact us;

*for inspiration, you'll be provided with a website link for all of the design elements we can incorporate within the WordPress website, through short codes; 

*Please let us know if you have any other questions!

*Est. project time of 2-5 hours;

Website link: rjwachsmanhomes.com

